h tempo and threats.\nReason: N: a8-b6 places the knight on an active outpost, attacks key central squares (c4/d5) and can hop to d7/c8/a4/c4 to create forks against the king and rooks, while also being safer and more influential than leaving it stuck on a8.\nAnswer: N: a8-b6'}
